                <pb facs="0744" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-03-05T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1925—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 6—9:08
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. My 31. March 4, 4 p.m. At conference at Aligandi, head chief of southern San
                    Bias region accepted Porvenir agreement and promised to abstain from further
                    proceedings. Am returning to Panama at once on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cleveland</hi>. Expect to arrive tomorrow afternoon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">South</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
